  - question: Is COPD the same as emphysema?
    answer: >-
      COPD is the umbrella name for a group of lung conditions, including
      emphysema (damage to the air sacs in the lungs) and chronic bronchitis
      (long-term swelling of the airways). Many people have both.
  - question: Is it too late to stop smoking if I have COPD?
    answer: >-
      No. Stopping smoking is the most effective way to slow COPD down, at
      any stage. Free help from a stop smoking service makes you much more
      likely to succeed.
